.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt NODE-UPDATE.SH 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm node-update.sh
.Nd verify and install a MANET tools update
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -routine
.Op Fl -development
.Op Fl -allow-downgrade
.Op Fl -recover-only | Fl -recover-files
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
selects the stable GitHub release marked Latest and installs the board's
tools archive if its version is newer.
Run it as root.
Downloads require qualified clock synchronization, recorded in
.Pa /run/initial_time_synced .
Without that marker, the command reports that the clock is not synced.
Local archive recovery does not require clock synchronization.
The archive digest, paths and embedded versions are checked before staging.
The tools archive may carry any component selected for the release,
including kernels, modules, firmware and configuration migrations.
Current packages update runtime files and managed radio firmware.
Kernel-specific installation, activation and boot recovery still require
implementation and validation before a kernel payload is shipped.
Follow the selected release's activation and reboot instructions.
.Pp
A pending installation resumes from its saved archive before checking
for a new release.
Individual files are replaced atomically, but the whole update has no
automatic rollback.
Errors are logged under the journal identifier
.Li manet-update .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -routine
Suppress console output and skip release checks for 24 hours after a
successful check or installation.
Pending recovery bypasses this delay.
.It Fl -development
Select the most recently published build, including prereleases,
for this invocation.
.It Fl -allow-downgrade
Allow the selected release to replace a newer installed version.
.It Fl -recover-only
Finish a pending update from local recovery files without networking.
Do nothing if no update is pending.
.It Fl -recover-files
Restore a pending payload before service startup, leaving final service
checks and completion to the later recovery pass.
Do nothing if no update is pending.
Cannot be combined with
.Fl -recover-only .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/manet_version.txt , /usr/local/bin/version.txt
Installed version markers.
.It Pa /var/lib/manet-update/
Staging and saved recovery data; an
.Pa in-progress
marker records unfinished installation.
.It Pa /run/manet-update.lock
Lock excluding concurrent updates.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 after an update or recovery succeeds, or when no work is needed,
including when another updater holds the lock.
Exits 1 on an operating error and 2 for invalid arguments.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Select the newest published build:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo node-update.sh --development
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr journalctl 1 ,
.Xr manet-provision-status.sh 8
